            <div xml:id="d798">

                <pb facs="0990" n="866" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg866"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.51/2240</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in the Dominican
                        Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Herod</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-12-23"><hi rendition="#italic">December 23,
                        1921</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 429</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: There is sent to you enclosed herein two
                    copies of the Department’s letter of December 17, 1921, to the Secretary of the
                    Navy, in reply to his request that this Government agree to a further loan <pb
                        facs="0991" n="867" xml:id="pg867"/> to the Dominican Republic of
                    $7,500,000. You will retain the carbon copy in the Legation files and transmit
                    the other copy to the Military Governor, under cover of a letter addressed
                    directly to him, for the information of the Dominican Government.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry P.
                            Fletcher</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d798-a1.xml" xpointer="d798-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
